<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Griffins</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Griffins, House of Griffin, Griffin dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Griffin was the dynasty that ruled the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a> from the 12th century until 1637. Its first historically attested member was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wartislaw-i-duke-of-pomerania">Wartislaw I</a>, who accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> in the 1120s. Of Slavic origin but German in culture by the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, the family often divided its lands into lines such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania-stettin">Pomerania-Stettin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania-wolgast">Pomerania-Wolgast</a>, and it died out with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogislaw-xiv">Bogislaw XIV</a> in 1637.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-griffins.jpg" alt="House of Griffins" width="320" height="369" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: N3MOUser:Artemis Andromeda · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:COA_Pomerania-Stettin_Iberian_style_shield_white.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>A <b>Griffin</b> prince, Eric of Pomerania, became king of Denmark, Norway and Sweden in 1397, and later ended his days as a minor duke in Pomerania.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-pomerania">Duchy of Pomerania · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>On his death in 1637 the <b>Griffin</b> line ended, and in 1648 the lands were divided between Swedish Pomerania and Brandenburg.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-pomerania-stettin">Duchy of Pomerania-Stettin</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1295 the <b>Griffin</b> brothers Bogislaw IV and Otto I divided the Duchy of Pomerania.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-pomerania-wolgast">Duchy of Pomerania-Wolgast</a></li></ul></section>
